    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0544" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg534"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 24.</seg></opener>
                <head>Lieutenant Governor Gordon to the Duke of Newcastle.—(Received February 16,
                    1864.)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frederickton</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 1, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord Duke:</hi> I have the honor to transmit for
                    your grace’s information a report of the evidence adduced in the case of the
                    Chesapeake, since the date of my last despatch on the subject.</p>
                <p>Your grace will probably be surprised to find an investigation commenced before
                    the police magistrate on the 28th of December still unconcluded.</p>
                <p>I have also the honor to enclose copies of further correspondence between the
                    Hon. J. H. Gray and myself.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ARTHUR H. GORDON.</signed></closer>




